# Intent: Train 6 item 3, dance extras beyond the four built-ins, as data. Six named dances (sway, nod_yes, shake_no, wiggle, bow, groove), each a short row of steps in maipai_dances_core.h: head yaw and pitch (tenths of a degree) with a servo speed, eye and mouth weight, an eye shift and a time per step. The firmware turns a row into the same keyframes the built-ins use (stackchan::animation::Keyframe) only while it plays (about 1 KB of heap, freed when the modifier ends); the table is flash data and no task or timer is added. Every row is checked against the limits the built-in dances stay inside (turn at most 60 degrees, tilt between -30 and +25, speed 50 to 1000, step 100 ms to 2 s, eight seconds in all, centred at both ends) and a row that fails is not played. self.robot.dance accepts the new names (it still plays one dance at a time, replacing a running one, and self.robot.stop_dance stops it) and self.robot.dance_list names every dance with its length. The word reactions keep their own four-dance list (their saved table format does not change).
# Placement: unit (the dances are played by the robot; the host asks for one by name)
# Upstream: firmware/main/hal/hal_mcp.cpp and stackchan/modifiers/dance.h of the StackChan main component (MIT); the new dances are MaiPai data in the same keyframe shape
# Check after a flash: self.robot.dance_list answers the four built-in names and six extras with their lengths; self.robot.dance with each extra name answers true and the head moves for about its length and ends centred; an unknown name answers false; self.robot.stop_dance ends one early.
